                      </chunks>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="param_output" index="5">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Latitude of the SITE in decimal degrees (north positive): the Latitude/Longitude inputs when BOTH are given, else the document's Earth Anchor Point (which also replaces a half-given pair); empty when neither gives a full site — half a site is not a site. NOT the weather station's position — that is Deconstruct Weather's Latitude, and a station can sit tens of km from the site (an airfield, usually, whose open land cover is the wrong answer). Wire it into Land Cover Roughness's Latitude so land cover and terrain are fetched where the model is. Available as soon as the site is known, before any file is downloaded.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">74cf75fa-10ce-468b-95b6-dbf57bbf5419</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Site Latitude</item>
                        <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Lat</item>
                        <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                        <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                      <chunks count="1">
                        <chunk name="Attributes">
